# Line endings are a property of the COMMIT, not of the machine that made it.
#
# Without this, normalisation depends on each contributor's `core.autocrlf`, and
# three tracks write this repo. Brief 018 paid for the same class once:
# `_fingerprint()` hashed raw bytes, so one commit hashed differently under
# different autocrlf settings and verifying a historical version needed a search
# over 2^n conventions. The fix there was to remove the degree of freedom.
* text=auto

# ONE file, not `*.json`. The web repo's `contract-in-sync` job (ci.yml:62)
# byte-diffs exactly this path against the canonical public copy; nothing else is
# compared byte for byte. Pinning every JSON would rewrite `hypotheses.json`,
# `candidates.json` and `web/slugs/nfl.json` in the working tree of a repo three
# tracks share - the cross-track rewrite this file exists to prevent. The
# vendored copy carries the same attribute on its side, so the guarantee holds
# from both ends.
web/contract/v2/contract.schema.json text eol=lf
